# **The first movie that reaches a level other than level 1**, and it gets there
# the way a player would: by typing a password.
#
# Every movie before this one begins by mashing Start through the logos and
# taking the title menu's first entry, which is level 1 and only ever level 1.
# That was the binding constraint on most of Phase 3's work list. Three separate
# items were marked *not reachable in level 1* rather than *not written yet* --
# `$80:F8D6`'s slot arithmetic wants collision id $28, which is behind a fence;
# `$80:FA26` wants id $2D, which is inside a hedge; and `enemy_survived` wants an
# enemy with health, which level 1's actor list does not place. All fourteen of
# its actors run `$81:87F8`, whose init is `LDA #$0000 : STA $1E`.
#
# **XJQY is level 33.** It is not guessed and it is not looked up: `$82:B018`
# reads a password out of four tables in bank $82, and `zamn_assets password`
# spells all 130 of them back out of the same tables --
#
#     build\zamn_assets.exe password "Zombies Ate My Neighbors.sfc"
#     build\zamn_assets.exe password "Zombies Ate My Neighbors.sfc" xjqy
#         XJQY -> level 33, victim gate 16 -- the level as it starts
#
# -- so any of the thirteen levels a password can name is now one command and
# one regenerate away. `docs/password.md` is the format.
#
# Level 33 is "Weird Kids on the Block", and what it has that level 1 does not
# is **enemies with health**: fourteen of its twenty-nine actors run `$81:8C17`,
# whose init is `LDA #$0004 : STA $1E`, against a damage table whose smallest
# non-zero entry is 1. Nothing here hits one yet -- the route to them is a maze
# and this movie stops at the first junction -- but they are three hundred
# pixels north of where Zeke stands, which is closer than any of them have ever
# been.
#
# What this movie is for right now is the structural question, and it answers
# it: **the port runs a level it has never seen.** Different tileset, different
# actor bodies, different music, 29 actors instead of 14 -- and `verify` checks
# every call without a single divergence or a single decline.
#
# Regenerate the boot half with:
#     python tools\make_password_movie.py XJQY
#
# Frames 0-1004 are level1.zmv's logo mashing. 1200-1268 takes the title menu's
# *second* entry. 1400-2056 walks the 7x5 character grid and types X, J, Q, Y
# and enter. The Start presses after that are the player-select screen.

